            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An internal combustion engine injector mounting (1700) is configured to i) secure an injector (36) to an internal combustion engine body (14) so that the injector can inject a heated aqueous fluid and a fuel into a combustion chamber (12) of the internal combustion engine, and ii) hold a catalyst (1714) so that the heated aqueous fluid and fuel are injected into the combustion chamber by passing through the catalyst. The catalyst is contained within the mounting to protect against oxidation by combustion processes that, in use, take place in the combustion chamber.</p>
            </abstract>
